OCCUPAI FUNCTION INVENTORY
==========================

Purpose
-------
This document lists the user-facing functions available in OccupAI.
It is organized for QA walkthroughs, demonstrations, and teacher review.

Platforms covered
-----------------
1. Admin Web   - template/dashboard.html
2. Driver Web  - template/driver.html
3. Admin App   - Flutter DashboardScreen using role=admin
4. Driver App  - Flutter DashboardScreen using role=driver

The technical reference sections identify implementation functions. Appendix A gives
teacher-ready summaries using the simple sample-style format.
Function names are included where the source has a named implementation.


1. AUTHENTICATION AND ACCOUNT ACCESS
====================================

These functions are shared by web roles and mobile roles.

| Function / workflow | Short description | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Sign in | Authenticates a user and starts the correct role dashboard. | Web login / LoginScreen |
| Role redirect | Sends administrators or drivers to their assigned dashboard. | login.html, register.html |
| Sign out | Revokes the session and returns the user to login. | Web signOut / DashboardScreen._logout |
| Registration | Creates a driver account with validated personal information. | register.html / RegisterScreen |
| Password validation | Requires eight characters, letters, and numbers before submission. | backend/models.py, register.dart |
| Forgot password | Requests a secure reset link without revealing account existence. | forgot-password pages / ForgotPasswordScreen |
| Reset password | Updates passwords using single-use, expiring reset tokens. | reset-password page / backend main.py |
| Session persistence | Stores mobile tokens securely and restores authenticated sessions. | ApiService secure storage |
| Session expiry handling | Clears invalid sessions and redirects users to login. | DashboardScreen, ApiService |


2. ADMIN WEB FUNCTIONS
======================

Source: template/dashboard.html. The admin web contains seven dashboard modules.

2.1 Navigation, access, and interface
--------------------------------------

| Function | Short description |
|---|---|
| switchPanel | Switches between the seven admin dashboard modules. |
| signOut | Clears the web session and redirects to login. |
| authHeaders | Builds authenticated headers for backend requests. |
| getStoredUser | Reads stored administrator display information. |
| fetchWithRetry | Retries failed requests using delayed backoff. |
| staggerCalls | Spaces network calls to reduce startup request bursts. |
| setSkeleton | Shows or hides loading placeholders. |
| setConnected | Updates the backend connection indicator. |
| applyTheme | Applies the selected dashboard theme. |
| initTheme | Restores the saved theme preference. |
| toggleTheme | Toggles the gray or dark interface theme. |
| isPanelActive | Checks whether an admin module is currently visible. |

2.2 Overview and live operations
--------------------------------

| Function | Short description |
|---|---|
| fetchStats | Retrieves current occupancy and camera statistics. |
| fetchHistory | Retrieves recent occupancy activity records. |
| renderHistory | Displays recent occupancy activity rows. |
| updateTrendChart | Draws the recent occupancy trend chart. |
| renderStatusVisual | Displays capacity, occupancy, and connection status. |
| renderTrendVisual | Displays historical occupancy movement visually. |
| renderForecastVisual | Displays near-term occupancy forecast visually. |
| renderZones | Displays occupied and available parking zones. |
| liveStatusText | Creates a readable current parking status label. |
| clampPct | Restricts percentages to safe display limits. |
| pctClass | Selects visual styling for occupancy percentages. |
| hourLabel24 | Formats a twenty-four-hour label for charts. |

2.3 Revenue and payment management
-----------------------------------

| Function | Short description |
